<overview>
<p>Ceremonial close combat platoons are honor guard formations trained primarily in melee weapons, carrying vibro-katanas or similar bladed arms alongside standard sidearms. These platoons serve as palace guards, diplomatic escorts, and formal security details where martial tradition and visual impression matter as much as combat readiness. Their close-quarters training gives them an edge in confined spaces, but they lack the ranged firepower of standard infantry platoons.</p>
</overview>

